Description: core: stereo3d_unpack keeps a deep source's bits
 The filter asked every producer for RGBA, 8 bits a sample, so a 10 bit clip taken
 apart in a producer (in_producer, a 3D clip in a Kdenlive project) lost its depth
 before the encoder, whatever the encoder asked for. When what asks for the frame
 wants more than 8 bits a sample (yuv420p10, yuv444p10, yuv422p16, rgba64), the
 filter now asks for RGBA64, copies, scales and fits the views at 16 bits a sample
 (the fitting sums in double, so a full alpha stays full), and hands back the
 format that was asked for. An opaque picture then carries no alpha mask: with
 the mask the conversion leaves, Kdenlive's track compositing (qtblend) took the
 picture as one with transparency and drew it black under Kdenlive's headless
 render (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen). An 8 bit request is served in RGBA as before;
 a frame sequence is still paired in RGBA.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
